<section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-blocks"><div class="fcx-block" style="grid-column:1/-1"><h2>Fan Section Solutions for HVAC Applications</h2><p>Fan sections are incorporated into ventilation and air-handling systems to provide controlled air movement. They help improve airflow distribution and support efficient operation in commercial, industrial, and public spaces.</p><p>Plug fans provide compact solutions by integrating directly into ductwork or equipment, while mixed flow fans integrate axial and centrifugal characteristics to offer balanced airflow and pressure performance.</p><p>For clients looking for <b>Plug Fans Manufacturer in Hyderabad</b>, the available solutions are designed for space-limited applications where efficient airflow delivery and reliable performance are required.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Plug Fans</h2></div><p class="fcx-lead">Plug fans are designed to integrate directly into ductwork or HVAC equipment. Their compact design makes them suitable for applications in which installation space is limited.</p><p class="fcx-lead">The current plug fan range includes adjustable pitch impellers and provides efficient airflow delivery for HVAC systems and industrial environments.</p><div class="fcx-cards fcx-cards--1"><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fan"></i></span><h3>Plug Fan Specifications</h3><ul class="fcx-mini"><li>Size range from 315 mm to 1600 mm</li><li>Capacity up to 1,30,000 CMH</li><li>Static pressure up to 40 mmWG</li><li>Adjustable pitch impeller</li><li>Compact installation design</li><li>Suitable for HVAC systems</li><li>Suitable for commercial applications</li><li>Efficient airflow delivery</li></ul></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-blocks"><div class="fcx-block" style="grid-column:1/-1"><h2>Mixed Flow Fans</h2><p>Mixed flow fans integrate the characteristics of axial and centrifugal fans. This design provides a balance between airflow volume and pressure performance, making them appropriate for different ventilation applications.</p><p>The backward-curved impeller design helps achieve higher efficiency and lower noise levels. These fans are appropriate for washrooms, hotels, auditoriums, stations, supermarkets, airports, and other public applications.</p><p>For projects requiring <b>Mixed Flow Fans Manufacturer in Hyderabad</b>, these fans can be selected for applications where efficient airflow, reduced noise, and reliable performance are vital considerations.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Key Features of Fan Sections</h2><p>The current fan section solutions offer:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>Plug fan and mixed flow fan configurations</li><li>Size range from 315 mm to 1600 mm for plug fans</li><li>Capacity up to 1,30,000 CMH</li><li>Static pressure up to 40 mmWG</li><li>Adjustable pitch impeller design</li><li>Backward-curved impeller technology</li><li>Compact installation options</li><li>Efficient airflow performance</li><li>Lower noise operation</li><li>Suitable for HVAC applications</li><li>Suitable for commercial ventilation systems</li><li>Suitable for industrial areas</li></ul></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><div class="fcx-tables"><div class="fcx-tablewrap"><table class="fcx-table"><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Product</th><td>Fan Sections</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Available Types</th><td>Plug Fans &amp; Mixed Flow Fans</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Plug Fan Size</th><td>315 mm – 1600 mm</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Capacity</th><td>Up to 1,30,000 CMH</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Static Pressure</th><td>Up to 40 mmWG</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Plug Fan Impeller</th><td>Adjustable Pitch</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mixed Flow Impeller</th><td>Backward Curved</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Main Applications</th><td>HVAC Systems, Ventilation &amp; Industrial Applications</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Design Focus</th><td>Airflow Efficiency, Noise Control &amp; Durability</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Applications in Hyderabad</h2><p>Hyderabad is a major commercial and industrial hub with pharmaceutical industries, IT parks, laboratories, manufacturing facilities, hospitals, hotels, and large commercial buildings. These sectors require reliable HVAC and ventilation solutions for maintaining proper indoor air movement.</p><p>Fan sections can be used in:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>Air handling units</li><li>HVAC systems</li><li>Industrial ventilation</li><li>Pharmaceutical facilities</li><li>Manufacturing plants</li><li>Hotels</li><li>Hospitals</li><li>Auditoriums</li><li>Airports</li><li>Railway stations</li><li>Supermarkets</li><li>Commercial buildings</li></ul><p><b>For Industrial Fan Sections Manufacturer in Hyderabad</b> requirements, selection should be based on airflow, static pressure, application, installation arrangement, and operating conditions.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Benefits of Fan Sections</h2></div><div class="fcx-cards fcx-cards--3"><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-screwdriver-wrench"></i></span><h3>Compact Installation</h3><p>Plug fans provide compact installation options by integrating directly into ductwork or HVAC equipment.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-gauge-high"></i></span><h3>Efficient Airflow Performance</h3><p>Fan sections are designed to offer reliable airflow distribution for different industrial and commercial applications.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-volume-xmark"></i></span><h3>Lower Noise Operation</h3><p>Mixed flow fans use backward-curved impellers to achieve better efficiency and lower noise levels.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-shapes"></i></span><h3>Flexible Configurations</h3><p>Different fan section options allow selection according to system requirements, available space, and airflow conditions.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-ruler-combined"></i></span><h3>Wide Application Range</h3><p>Fan sections can support HVAC systems, industrial processes, and public-space ventilation requirements.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-blocks"><div class="fcx-block"><h2>How to Select the Right Fan Section</h2><p>The selection of a fan section depends on airflow requirement, static pressure, application, and installation conditions.</p><p>For HVAC systems, factors such as equipment size, available space, air volume, and pressure requirement should be considered.</p><p>For commercial applications, operating environment, vibration, noise, durability, and maintenance requirements must also be evaluated.</p><p><b>For Fan Sections Manufacturer in India</b>, customers should provide airflow details, pressure requirements, application information, and project conditions for correct technical selection.</p></div><div class="fcx-block"><h2>Manufacturing and Supply for Hyderabad</h2><p>The fan sections are manufactured at the Neemrana, Rajasthan facility and supplied to Hyderabad and other places throughout India. Each unit is chosen according to airflow requirements, static pressure, and project conditions.</p><p>For customers looking for <b>Fan Sections Supplier in Hyderabad</b>, providing complete project details helps determine the appropriate fan configuration and technical specifications.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div><div class="fcx-faq"><details><summary>What are fan sections used for?</summary><p>Fan sections are used in HVAC systems, air handling units, industrial ventilation, and commercial airflow applications.</p></details><details><summary>What types of fan sections are available?</summary><p>The current range includes plug fans and mixed flow fans.</p></details><details><summary>What is the size range of plug fans?</summary><p>Plug fans are available in a 315 mm to 1600 mm size range.</p></details><details><summary>What is the capacity of plug fans?</summary><p>The listed capacity is up to 1,30,000 CMH with static pressure up to 40 mmWG.</p></details><details><summary>Where are mixed flow fans used?</summary><p>Mixed flow fans are used in washrooms, hotels, auditoriums, stations, supermarkets, airports, and other public applications.</p></details></div><div class="fcx-center" style="margin-top:26px"><a href="product.php" class="btn-cyber btn-cyber--primary fcx-btn" title="Fan Air India Products">Learn More <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-cta"><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Fan sections provide efficient airflow solutions for HVAC systems, industrial ventilation, and commercial applications. With plug fan and mixed flow fan configurations, adjustable pitch impellers, compact designs, and reliable airflow performance, they support specific project requirements.</p><p>FanAir India Pvt. Ltd. manufactures fan sections at its Neemrana facility and supplies them to Hyderabad and other locations throughout India.</p><a href="../contact.php" class="fcx-cta__btn" title="Contact Fan Air India">Contact Us <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section>
